                <pb facs="0724" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./656:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-17T17:00:00-04:00">September 17, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Your 148, September 13, 8 p.m. It is Colonel Lindbergh’s plan to stop in
                    Venezuela on his return flight from Paramaribo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
